{
  "1": [
    {
      "text": "American silver eagles and Canadian",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.74
    },
    {
      "text": "maple leaves are the most recognizable",
      "startSec": 1.74,
      "endSec": 3.3
    },
    {
      "text": "silver you can buy.",
      "startSec": 3.3,
      "endSec": 4.72
    },
    {
      "text": "That recognition comes with a price,",
      "startSec": 4.72,
      "endSec": 6.4
    },
    {
      "text": "typically 18-25% above spot.",
      "startSec": 6.4,
      "endSec": 9.12
    },
    {
      "text": "You are paying for the government mint,",
      "startSec": 9.12,
      "endSec": 11.04
    },
    {
      "text": "the guaranteed purity, and the fact",
      "startSec": 11.04,
      "endSec": 12.55
    },
    {
      "text": "that any dealer in the country will buy",
      "startSec": 12.55,
      "endSec": 13.86
    },
    {
      "text": "them back on the spot.",
      "startSec": 13.86,
      "endSec": 15.12
    }
  ],
  "2": [
    {
      "text": "Generic silver rounds are privately",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.06
    },
    {
      "text": "minted, one Troy ounce, 99.9% fine",
      "startSec": 2.06,
      "endSec": 4.74
    },
    {
      "text": "silver.",
      "startSec": 4.74,
      "endSec": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "The only thing missing is the",
      "startSec": 6,
      "endSec": 7.19
    },
    {
      "text": "government stamp, and the premium",
      "startSec": 7.19,
      "endSec": 9.52
    },
    {
      "text": "reflects that.",
      "startSec": 9.52,
      "endSec": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "At 4-8% above spot, rounds give you",
      "startSec": 10,
      "endSec": 12.26
    },
    {
      "text": "more silver for the same money with",
      "startSec": 12.26,
      "endSec": 13.62
    },
    {
      "text": "nearly the same storage and stacking",
      "startSec": 13.62,
      "endSec": 14.93
    },
    {
      "text": "properties as coins.",
      "startSec": 14.93,
      "endSec": 16
    }
  ],
  "3": [
    {
      "text": "Bars take premiums even lower. 2 to 3",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.42
    },
    {
      "text": "percent on 10-ounce bars in normal",
      "startSec": 2.42,
      "endSec": 4.4
    },
    {
      "text": "market conditions.",
      "startSec": 4.4,
      "endSec": 5.68
    },
    {
      "text": "The trade-off is divisibility. A 10-",
      "startSec": 5.68,
      "endSec": 7.9399999999999995
    },
    {
      "text": "ounce bar is one piece you cannot split,",
      "startSec": 7.9399999999999995,
      "endSec": 9.92
    },
    {
      "text": "so the lowest premium option is not",
      "startSec": 9.92,
      "endSec": 11.5
    },
    {
      "text": "always the most flexible one,",
      "startSec": 11.5,
      "endSec": 12.8
    },
    {
      "text": "especially if you might need to sell a",
      "startSec": 12.8,
      "endSec": 14.36
    },
    {
      "text": "part of your position later.",
      "startSec": 14.36,
      "endSec": 15.76
    }
  ],
  "4": [
    {
      "text": "The full comparison of all three,",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.07
    },
    {
      "text": "including which to buy first, is linked",
      "startSec": 2.07,
      "endSec": 3.82
    },
    {
      "text": "in the comments.",
      "startSec": 3.82,
      "endSec": 4.46
    }
  ]
}